[#:seon.task{:name "delivered-errors-carry-no-result-handle",
            :plan
            "A core error recorded during an agent's call (another thread included) reaches the reply's `:seon.repl/errors` as `seon.error/value` plus count and branch, but with no result handle or dig form: the agent can reach the whole recorded error only by knowing to pull [`:seon.error/signature` s] with the observation selector. Reproduce: in SCI as agent X, @(future (`seon.fault/fault!` env (ex-info \"async\" {:probe/async 1}) {`:seon.agent/id` X ...})) answers :errors [{`:seon.error/signature` … `:seon.error/message` \"async\"}] without :probe/async or any handle. Correct (errors spec, 'Every error in a reply's :errors and :diagnostics carries its result handle'): each delivered error carries a handle or requery form that answers the whole recorded value. Proof: an evaluation that records a core fault answers :errors whose handle reads the fault's ex-data. Read `seon.render.transcript/branch-errors` and `seon.turn/fault-window`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "contract-runtime-duration"
             :plan "Give `seon.render.transcript/runtime-duration` a complete Malli contract that checks what its boundary is for, with the cheapest schema that checks it: registered names, every input and output, the error variants it returns. A contract that refuses a real value (a reaching test, a live call, your probe) is a finding, not friction: if the contract misread the value's shape, fix the contract and cite the observed shape; if the producer emits a bad value, keep the contract, send root the finding with `my.message/send`, naming `seon.render.transcript/runtime-duration` with the exact form, the refused value's essence and the Malli explain, and say so in your reply. Never widen to :any, [:maybe ...] or :map to go green. Done when `seon.contracts/gaps` answers [] for it and its reaching tests stay green and no slower. Read `docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "one-evaluation-reads-one-way"
             :plan "An evaluation is shown three ways. The model pass, the transcript and the debug view now share the exchange render (`seon.context/exchange-ai`, `seon.context/exchange-html` over `:seon.context/exchange`), but the evaluation entity's own pair (`seon.repl/render-ai`, `seon.repl/render-html`, with `seon.repl/text` and `seon.repl/render-emission-html`) still prints every evaluation as the newest, with the turn's meta, so an older model exchange reads differently there than in the model's history. And the transcript's exchanges carry the branch errors `seon.render.transcript/with-errors` sets as `:seon.repl/errors`, which `seon.context/exchange-values` never reads, so the page shows errors in an older reply that the model was not sent. Decide one producer of the emission (errors included or not) for both, and make the evaluation entity's pair the exchange render at its age (`seon.repl` cannot require `seon.context`: move the exchange render to the namespace both read, or move the age rule `seon.context/exchange-age` down to `seon.repl`)."}]
